[Music]  the Republican nominee in Georgia's  super close race for governor wants the  FBI to investigate alleged hacking by  Democrats Brian Kemp is also Georgia's  Secretary of State his office says in a  statement we open an investigation into  the Democratic Party of Georgia after  receiving information from our legal  team about failed efforts to breach the  online voter registration system Georgia  Democrats say the allegations are false  Kemp didn't mention the issue during  President Trump's political rally in  Macon Georgia yesterday but made a  last-minute plea to voters I cannot do  this without you the radical left is  pouring millions into Georgia they're  energized they're energized they're  mobilized their itching  they are itching you all the turn  Georgia into California Stacey Abrams is  the Democratic candidate for governor  and former House Minority Leader for the  state assembly she's with us from  Savannah we invited Secretary of State  kam to appear and he declined  good morning Stacey Abrams I want to  start with these allegations which  revolve around an email exchange has the  FBI or Homeland Security contacted your  campaign or the Democratic Party as far  as you know they have not and let's be  clear Brian Kemp was informed of this  flaw in his security system on Friday he  failed to act and instead on Sunday  without any evidence decided to try to  cast aspersions on Democrats we have  nothing to do with this this is yet  another example of his failure to secure  the information of more than 6 million  voters he has failed at this twice  already and we know that when he gets  caught he blames everyone else this lack  of accountability is not infinite of  anything other than his failure to do  his job there is no evidence there is  there's no there's not even a  conversation about Democrats having  anything to do with this other than  learning along with everyone else that  Brian Kemp had failed once again to be  the effective secretary do you think  it's gonna affect the vote come Tuesday  what I think will happen is that once  again this shows a pattern of voter  suppression on the part of Brian Kemp  trying to scare people out of casting  their votes but we've been working hard  for 18 months to increase the sense of  security that people should have about  our democracy writ large and we know the  best antidote  - voter suppression is voter engagement  and that's why we're excited about the  overwhelming number of people who turned  out an early voting already in Georgia  and we intend to see them there on  Election Day are you concerned about the  fairness of this election I'm concerned  that there is someone seeking  advancement to higher office having  failed to do this fundamental job as the  guardian of the public trust of our  democracy Brian Kemp does not deserve a  promotion however I'm not gonna focus on  him alone I'm focusing on the voters of  Georgia talking about education about  jobs about expanding Medicaid because if  they will cast their ballots and voice  their concerns about these issues we  will have a fair election because so  many of us will vote there will be no  question about the outcome you know  president Trump is you know Stacey  Abrams campaigned in Macon Georgia  yesterday he said this about you  described you as one of the most extreme  left-wing opponents saying that if you  put Stacey in there you'll have Georgia  turn into Venezuela so how are you  dealing with comments like that about  you and your campaign  I told tell people to look at my record  I'm the only candidate in this race  who's worked across the aisle who's  gotten a ratings from the Georgia  Chamber of Commerce and the friend of  labor award I'm the only one with  detailed plans on how we improve access  to education in the state of Georgia how  we cover half a million people with  access to affordable health care and how  we create good-paying jobs across the  state of Georgia my opponent doesn't  have a record what he has is rhetoric  and failed policies and failed behavior  and so I think when people look at my  record and they look at my plans they  will know that I'm the only candidate  who has their best interest at heart but  did you know voters don't often do a  deep deep dive they look at the  headlines and Brian camp is saying about  you that this is a forest this this is a  distraction there are counter charges  back and forth what do you do to keep  people focused who are just sort of sick  of both sides now at this point well I  would say this I think that what's  happened over the last few months is  that Brian camp has consistently behaved  in a way that is not worthy of this  office and what voters have seen is not  a back-and-forth they've seen one person  who throws out desperate attacks who has  to basically blame everyone else for his  failures and I've run a consistent  campaign and I've never pointed a  shotgun at anyone I've never blown  anything up I've been talking about the  same three issues since the day I  launched his campaign good jobs good  healthcare and good education for our  kids referring there to images that  Brian Kemp had in his campaign but  statement you said there's no evidence  but isn't the Kemp campaign pointing to  an email exchange in which there was  discussion of vulnerabilities in the  state's system isn't that what they're  saying is the evidence so let's be clear  there was an email sent by our voter  Protection Division to cyber security  folks because they'd receive this  information and we did the right thing  which is we got information that there  was a vulnerability we sent it to  cybersecurity folks because it's the  voter Protection Division of our  campaign but the issue was that Brian  Kemp was told about this days before and  did nothing to alert the public to the  fact that there was another flaw and hit  the system he's responsible for  overseeing and instead of addressing the  flaw and taking responsibility he  decided to go to a desperate place and  blame Democrats for simply alerting  cybersecurity experts  to his failure okay Stacey Abrams we're  gonna have to leave it there thank you  again we invited Secretary of State  Brian Kem to appear and he declined our  invitation

